Patch summary:
Add the ScanoutDmabufExport renderer feature. When enabled (the default),
stream_renderer_resource_get_info describes color buffers (format, the
driver's row pitch) so the VMM can scan them out as dma-bufs; when disabled
it returns EINVAL for color buffers, rutabaga records no 3D info and crosvm
keeps reading the scanout back. The VMM's display imports the exported image
with an implicit layout (no DRM modifier), which only works where the driver
leaves the layout in the buffer: RADV (BO metadata) and the host GL drivers
(GEM tiling). ANV does not (Intel HD 6000: the console came out as horizontal
bands), and the udmabuf path (Apple Silicon) has no such information. So the
default is off on the udmabuf path, and on Vulkan hosts the info is only
given when the driver is RADV, unless --gpu_renderer_features overrides the
feature explicitly, which is honored as given.

